193
00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:12.010
I'll explain.

194
00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.510
First of all, I have a creative journal.

195
00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:22.170
Now, this is where I write down quotes from books that I feel like might inspire me in the future

196
00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:26.750
if I'm working on a creative project, like maybe for a character I'm playing or something.

197
00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:28.550
Oh, that's so you.

198
00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:29.650
And I just love it.

199
00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:34.610
But I'll also have an observation and it'll go in my creative journal.

200
00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:39.430
Like this morning, I set my to-go coffee on the hood of my car.

201
00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:45.650
And then when I got in my car, I had to open my door and get it because I'd forgotten it.

202
00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:48.730
And it was a little too far for me to reach, but I could reach it.

203
00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:49.830
Did you spill it?

204
00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:50.970
No, I didn't spill it.

205
00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:57.950
But what I thought was, oh my God, if I ever have to play a character who puts her coffee on her hood,

206
00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:03.170
I should put it a little too far because it's more realistic that you have to reach for it.

207
00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:04.550
I'm going to make a note of that.

208
00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:07.830
I'll put that in my creative journal and I'll unpack that sometime.

209
00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:11.030
So if you ever see me in a movie reaching for a coffee on the hood of my car,

210
00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:12.930
you'll know where it came from.

211
00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:15.930
This is very much like sort of the artist in you.

212
00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.010
Oh my goodness.

213
00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:20.530
Well, anyway, so that's a pen and paper journal.

214
00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:22.250
I also have a personal journal.

215
00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:25.850
That's where I try to process like life stuff.

216
00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:26.170
Yeah.

217
00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:27.530
That's also pen and paper.

218
00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.670
For that journal, I love a prompt.

219
00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:31.830
There's a lot that you can find on the internet.

220
00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:35.410
So sometimes I'll look up a prompt and I'll use that for my personal journal.

221
00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:40.690
But I also have a journal for each of my kids and I keep those on my computer.

222
00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:44.550
And I go to it from time to time and I just write about them.

223
00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.210
It's something that I want to give them when they're older.

224
00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:54.030
And I'm really glad I did this because when I scroll back to an entry from when they were like wee little,

225
00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:57.950
I will have recorded some funny phrase they said.

226
00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:01.990
Or like the name of their treasured stuffed animal at the time.

227
00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:06.130
And it's stuff that you think you will never forget, but I had actually forgotten.

228
00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:06.930
You do though.

229
00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:07.490
You do.

230
00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:08.130
You forget.

231
00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:08.890
Yes.

232
00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:11.590
And I so wish that I had written even more.

233
00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.230
But I'm grateful that I did it at all.

234
00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:17.310
And I'm always backing it up and printing it out and making sure that it doesn't get loSt.

235
00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:20.190
You know, that's like my one anxiety about that journal.

236
00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:24.890
But then I also have a separate travel journal, which is also on my computer.

237
00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:28.050
And I love making photo albums of our travels.

238
00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:31.590
And then I include the travel journal in the photo album.

239
00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:37.550
So yes, I have a lot of journals and a lot of habits and organization for my journals, Alex.

240
00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:42.310
Well, I guess I wasn't really thinking about some of the other things that I sort of document.

241
00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:45.710
But I had a journal given to me as a gift.

242
00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:50.830
This is a great gift, by the way, if you have a friend or family member who's having a baby.

243
00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:55.170
I was given a journal and it was like quote of the day from your kid.

244
00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:55.530
Oh, yeah.

245
00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:56.790
One line a day journal.

246
00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:57.270
Yes.

247
00:10:57.410 --> 00:10:57.630
Yeah.

248
00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:00.510
And I went in and wrote all these fun things.

249
00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:01.250
And I still have that.

250
00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:02.890
And Isabel and I just love it.

251
00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:04.510
We go back through it from time to time.

252
00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:08.930
And then actually, I did this thing, lady, because, you know, I have all my digital clutter.

253
00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:15.130
